\[
 p_{n,g}=g^2q_n[1+O(g^2)]+\text{exponentially small cutoff correction}.
\]

Parity cancels the weighted linear term in a smooth transverse multiplier. Its quadratic error has numerator \(O(g^4)\) and denominator of order \(g^2\), giving \(O(g^2)\). The root's proof is sound with this accounting. The sentence calling normalization errors exponential must refer only to cutoff-induced errors; the sine-weight normalization correction itself is algebraic. This is the second accepted wording correction.

