\]

This is the correct Hamiltonian test of \(\kappa\mathcal D[B_j]\). The second term is the real anticommutator pairing with \(B_j^*B_j\), not generally \(p_{n,g}\langle h\rangle_\Psi\). For the actual smooth finite-g packets, all indicated pairings exist: finite shift multipliers preserve smooth electric Sobolev vectors, and D is quadratic. The statement has not evaluated this power, assigned a reservoir Hamiltonian, or given a trajectorywise spectral heat measurement. No conversion of the conditional mean difference into heat per event is licensed.

